# {{senseid|pt|pronoun}} {{lb|pt|third person personal}} [[them]] (''as a direct object''; ''the corresponding indirect object is [[lhes]]''; ''the form used after prepositions is [[elas]]'')
#: {{syn|pt|las|nas}}
#: {{ux|pt|Encontrei-as na rua.|inline=1|I met them in the street.}}

====Usage notes====
* {{m|pt|as}} becomes -{{m|pt|las}} after verb forms ending in ''-r, -s'', or ''-z'', the pronouns {{m|pt|nos}} and {{m|pt|vos}}, and the adverb {{m|pt|eis}}; the ending letter causing the change disappears.
*: After {{m|pt|ver}}: {{ux|inline=1|pt|Posso vê-las?|May I see them?}}
*: After {{m|pt|pôr}}: {{ux|inline=1|pt|Quero pô-las ali.|I want to put them there.}}
*: After {{m|pt|fazer|fiz}}: {{ux|inline=1|pt|Fi-las ficar contente.|I made them become happy.}}
*: After {{m|pt|nos}}: {{ux|inline=1|pt|Deu-no-las relutantemente.|He gave them to us reluctantly.}}
*: After {{m|pt|eis}}: {{ux|inline=1|pt|Ei-las!|Behold them!}}
* Becomes -{{m|pt|nas}} after a nasal diphthong: ''-ão, -am'' [ɐ̃w̃], ''-õe'' [õj̃], ''-em, -êm'' [ẽj̃].
*: {{ux|pt|Detêm-nas como prisioneiros.|inline=1|They detain them as prisoners.}}
* In Brazil it is being abandoned in favor of the nominative form {{m|pt|elas}}.
*: ''Eu as vi.'' → ''Eu vi elas.'' = "I saw them.

